There are two thing in any programing language.
1. Hot code [A code which is getting executed repetitively][Like calling the function inside the for loop - infinite time,1000 times, function is getting executed n number of times in the for loop, so we need/required more processing to do that, that is called the Hot/warm code][This particuler code executed repetitively]
2. Cold code  [We don't need to do much processing] [Simple variable,basic loop, sum program -  then simply run it - that's it]

Everything[From SRC writing to OUTPUT] is happning within the v8 engine
V8 says you give us the AST tree that you have created now  we will decide 
> what/which is hot code and what/which is normal/cold code 
V8 will automatically recognize whether code is hot/cold

If code is a cold code then > simply interpret your code > convert it to machine code >machine code >output
But if there is a hot code [execution is happning again and again/reading a big file/] > then V8 engine says that "compilations" process comes into the picture > compilation is called "optimization processs"/ "profiling process"
So they will improve the pro-activitiy here
So now/thats why JIT comes into the picture [JIT - just in time]

in every programing language there is concept called JIT
JIT will be activated whenever we see > hey there is a hot code 
In java just in time is available 
[JIT] will improve your bytecode
[JIT] will introduce some catalyst 
[JIT] will improve your pro-activity
[JIT] will improve the performance of your execution 

JIT is a kind of compiler.
JIT will be activated when there is a hot/warm code 
If it is a hot/warm code  then JIT will come into the picture and will optimize your code 
And if your categorize your hot code into two particuler
1. less hot [warm code] 
2. very hot

1. less hot code needs less optimization[store] > converting code to machine code > machine code > output
2. Very hot code then > we will do the proper optimization [optimization] > converting code to machine code > machine code > output

They use few terms in javascript here
So whenever there is a hot code > just try to understand like a normal car, when we drive the car in the peak summer season (40 degree outside) and we are going for a trip 
> after 100,200 km engine will get hot/hit up > so we need to fill some cold water
> exactly we need to do over here fill some cold water/ we need to start the turbo engine. To cool down the system
> similar kind of terms used in javascript also  - which is - turbo fan - to cool down the system - then do "optimization" > converting code to machine code > machine code > output
> If there is a lot of hot code/warm code then "turbo fan" will start

